+## 6. Process lessons (feeds #1786 lease SSOT and the triage lane)
+
+1. **Stale claim labels mislead.** #1617 showed status:claimed from a lease
+   that expired 14 hours earlier; the label persisted while the lease died.
+   Triage agents reading labels alone would skip a live P1. The claim-lease
+   SSOT fix (#1786, in gates) addresses exactly this class.
+2. **Closed-unmerged does not mean content-lost.** The fleet has two landing
+   lanes (bridge PRs and the sync lane); #1656 died on one and its content
+   arrived on the other. Any rescue decision needs a byte-level re-probe of
+   the CURRENT tree, not the PR's patch text. (Same lesson family as the
+   #1911 r2 rebase-rescue.)
+3. **The 30-minute claim TTL is honest; labels are not.** Recommend the
+   bridge clear the status:claimed label when a lease lapses (admin lane,
+   bridge-core).
+
